  message: "DONE — the coordinate-vs-namespace import-pattern fix landed for every language that supports it (PR 64bae43c6e, dev 64bae43c6e). Added the real import namespaces: Scala play->play.api, akka-http->akka.http, zio-http->zio.http; Haskell scotty->Web.Scotty (JVM spring-boot was already fixed by WI-tolap). Each is dotted (promotes with no manifest via _is_specific_pattern) and scoped past the base library (akka.http not akka, zio.http not zio), with FP-guard tests that base-library imports (akka.actor, zio.ZIO) do NOT promote the HTTP framework. Behavioral: manifest-less 'import play.api.mvc._' -> frameworks []->[play]; 'import Web.Scotty' -> [scotty]. 275 test_profile.py tests pass; core 100% coverage. SCOPE RESOLUTION: (1) finatra is NOT dark — its com.twitter coord happens to prefix-match com.twitter.finatra.* imports — so no fix needed. (2) PHP (laravel/symfony/cakephp/yii/slim) is a DEEPER gap than a missing pattern (php.py emits no import edges for 'use' statements + the matcher has no backslash-namespace rule) — split out to INV-naguv, which owns the full PHP import-promotion chain. This item's coordinate-vs-namespace thesis is discharged for all import-emitting languages."  # b723
